WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.420
Kicking off the week on Tesla Short's time, episode 554 for July 27th, 2026, I'm Patrick

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:12.100
coming to you from Vancouver, a new week and plenty happening with Tesla.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.980
Macao's separate legal framework lets Tesla deliver GROC to owners there while mainland

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.720
China waits on licensing.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:25.740
Tesla posted record vehicle deliveries in the latest quarter, while automotive gross margins

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:26.340
narrowed.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:32.360
Pricing adjustments and higher operating expenses drove the compression even as unit volume

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:32.740
rose.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:39.060
The company continues to direct substantial capital toward autonomy, robotics, and energy

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.220
storage programs.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:45.820
Those initiatives have not yet generated revenues sufficient to offset the margin pressure.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.400
Investors are watching whether the delivery momentum can stabilize cash flow in coming

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:51.860
quarters.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:57.800
From the volume versus profit tension, regulatory quirks are already shaping how quickly

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.960
new software features reach customers.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:07.000
Tesla owners in Macao are already receiving the 2026.26 summer update that includes

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.000
GROC integration.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.480
The rollout works because Macao operates under a separate legal and internet framework

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.800
from mainland China under one country to systems.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.960
This arrangement lets XAI bypass the special government licensing required elsewhere in

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:23.440
the country.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:29.160
The update arrives through the normal over-the-air channel and requires no additional hardware

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.500
on supported vehicles.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:36.240
The same codebase remains unavailable on the mainland, pending formal approvals.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:42.720
While software features navigate regional rules, Tesla is also quietly expanding its AI

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.740
capabilities through acquisitions.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:50.980
Tesla completed an undisclosed AI-related acquisition without releasing further information.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:56.920
The move adds to the company's growing set of AI capabilities across vehicle and robotics

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:57.660
programs.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:03.280
No purchase price, target company name, or integration timeline has been disclosed in

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.560
regulatory filings or public statements.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.260
The transaction follows a pattern of smaller tuck-in deals aimed at strengthening internal

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.920
machine learning infrastructure.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:19.700
Any material contribution is expected to appear in future updates to cortex or dojo workloads.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:25.820
As Tesla builds its AI stack, questions about near-term returns are surfacing around

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.040
its humanoid robot.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.000
Investors questioned whether optimists can generate meaningful revenue soon.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.240
Elon Musk dismissed competing humanoid demos as staged during the exchange.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:44.200
Musk emphasized that Tesla's internal testing focuses on useful tasks rather than choreographed

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:44.600
displays.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.980
This follows yesterday's discussion on optimist production targets and keeps attention

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.620
on when visible factory output will begin.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:58.960
The debate centers on whether early units will first serve Tesla's own factories or external

00:02:58.960 --> 00:02:59.360
buyers.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:05.280
Shares of Hong Kong robotics companies climbed on expectations that optimists will reach

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.460
mass production before the end of the year.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:13.620
Component suppliers tied to actuators, sensors, and battery packs saw the largest gains.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.460
The optimism stems from Tesla's repeated statements that low-volume builds will begin

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:24.180
in late 2026, ahead of higher rate output in 2027.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:30.860
While optimist timelines draw scrutiny, the semi-program is also facing a clear regulatory

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:31.420
delay.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:37.920
Elon Musk stated that unsupervised self-driving capability for the Tesla semi remains about

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:38.760
a year away.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:44.660
Production of the supervised version continues at Giga, Texas, with early fleet customers

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:48.600
still evaluating range and payload economics on real roads.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:54.240
Musk's comment came during a public appearance and aligns with the company's broader caution

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:57.740
on regulatory approval for unsupervised operation.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:03.780
Fleets are therefore planning diesel replacement decisions around 2027 or later.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:09.720
While autonomy timelines affect more than just trucks, the latest customer software update

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.080
is already rolling out new driving features.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:18.440
The 2026 summer update adds new traction control modes aimed at improving handling across

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.400
different conditions.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:25.880
It reaches Model 3 and Model Y first, the vehicles that previously lacked dedicated drive

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.480
modes for varied surfaces.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:33.500
The feature set includes selectable settings for snow, sand, and off-road use that adjust

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.700
motor torque and stability systems in real-time.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.440
Owners can access the modes through the existing drive mode menu on the center screen.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:49.760
Roll-out began with vehicles already on the 2026.26 software branch and will continue

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.260
over the next several weeks.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:57.400
On-road software keeps improving and owners are already reporting strong low-speed performance

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.380
in the latest FSD release.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:08.040
An owner reported that FSD version 14.3.6 navigated a busy sheet slot, handled cars at gas

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.940
pumps and completed both outbound and home parking without issues.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:17.640
Multiple stops during the same drive showed consistent low-speed maneuvering around moving

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.300
vehicles and tight spaces.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:25.240
The same owner noted the system found spots in a packed target lot and repeated the result

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.540
at another shopping center the same morning.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:34.240
The software identified open spaces, executed precise reverse maneuvers, and avoided pedestrians

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.600
without driver input.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:41.940
A follow-up post confirmed zero parking problems encountered across multiple stops with varying

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:42.680
lot layouts.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:47.940
The consistency suggests incremental gains in low-speed navigation logic.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:55.520
Independent tests recorded the Rivian R2 using 18-26% more electricity per mile than

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.140
the Model Y under comparable conditions.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:05.440
The Rivian R2 carries the same official EPA efficiency rating as the Tesla Model Y, yet

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.940
real-world testing showed the R2 consuming more energy.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:14.320
The discrepancy highlights differences between laboratings and on-road performance for

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.060
the two vehicles.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:20.060
The gap appears most pronounced on highways and during cold weather drives.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:25.860
Rivian has not yet commented on the test methodology or potential software updates to close

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.420
the difference.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:32.480
Elon Musk appeared on the NELK Boys full-send podcast for a wide-ranging discussion.

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:38.440
The appearance provided another public forum for Tesla-related topics outside traditional

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:39.240
earnings calls.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:45.120
Listeners heard Musk addressed timelines for autonomy, robotics, and energy storage

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:46.880
in a conversational format.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:52.220
The episode reached a younger audience segment that may not follow quarterly financial

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:52.740
updates.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.600
No new product announcements were made during the conversation.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:02.540
Revenue trends for Ford and Tesla showed Tesla closing the gap with the larger automaker

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:03.780
in 2026.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:09.620
The comparison places Tesla's top-line growth against an established competitor's longer

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:10.940
operating history.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:17.200
Tesla's automotive and energy revenue combined now represent a meaningful fraction of Ford's

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.720
total despite fewer legacy product lines.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:25.800
The analysis notes that Tesla's services and regulatory credit streams contribute a

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.940
larger share of profit than equivalent segments at Ford.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:35.560
Both companies face margin pressure from EV transition costs, yet Tesla's growth rate

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:37.760
remains higher on a percentage basis.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:44.680
Services revenue rose 50%, yet the analysis concludes the stock valuation remains elevated

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.020
relative to that growth.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:50.800
The piece weighs the service's contribution against overall share pricing.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:56.960
Growth in the segment stems from increased supercharger utilization, insurance uptake,

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:58.720
and connectivity subscriptions.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:04.720
Even with the jump, the valuation multiple applied to the services line exceeds those of

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:07.320
comparable software or aftermarket businesses.

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:12.520
The report suggests investors are still pricing in substantial future contributions

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.180
from autonomy and robotics that have not yet materialized.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:21.620
While vehicle software advances, energy products are running into real world configuration

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:22.220
hurdles.

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:29.100
A UK customer preparing to install a Powerwall 3 had one battery unit disabled by Tesla,

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.840
which then initiated a recall replacement.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:37.780
Tesla remotely limited the unit's operation after detecting an anomaly during pre-installation

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:38.160
checks.

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:43.700
The owner was notified through the Tesla app and scheduled for a swap at no cost.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:49.380
A California homeowner installed a Powerwall specifically to avoid peak rate charges

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:55.240
under NEM 3.0 rules, only to observe the unit drawing power from the grid.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:09:00.980
Telemetry showed grid imports during periods when solar production should have covered household

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:06.960
load. Tesla support is investigating whether firmware settings or inverter logic require

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:14.740
adjustment for NEM 3.0 compliance. Energy hyphen product friction highlights the same regulatory

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:20.300
fragmentation that affects software rollouts. Regional regulatory differences can

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:26.000
accelerate or block software feature rollouts even when the underlying hardware and code are

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:31.960
identical. Tesla's GROC integration reached Macao owners first because the territories

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:37.620
separate legal and internet rules bypass the licensing process required on the mainland.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:43.920
That single distinction turns a uniform product into a staggered release schedule across one

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:49.880
country. The same pattern appears in energy products where local rate structures and interconnection

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:55.520
rules shape real world performance. Configuration files and firmware branches therefore

00:09:55.520 --> 00:10:02.100
multiply, raising the cost of testing and customer service staffing. For Tesla, the result is a

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:07.360
fragmented deployment map where features and hardware reach customers at different speeds depending

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:13.780
on local rules rather than engineering readiness alone. That fragmentation raises the cost of

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:19.460
support, testing, and customer communication while slowing the revenue recognition tied to each

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:26.300
new capability. Tesla achieved record deliveries while profitability fell. The gap shows that higher

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:33.000
volume alone has not offset rising costs or pricing pressure. The company continues to invest heavily

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:38.420
in AI, robotics, and autonomy programs that have yet to generate offsetting revenue.

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:44.860
Margin compression appears across both automotive and energy segments, leaving less cash for the

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:51.160
very initiatives driving the spending. Management has signaled that near-term results will remain volatile

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:57.280
until new product lines reach meaningful scale. Before we go, keep an eye on whether the next

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:03.480
FSD update extends the low speed consistency seen in parking lots to more highway scenarios.

